& [ReusableMechanics]
  + LiveCodexConfig pins the Codex executable Cantor MCP executable environment file and working directory by absolute path metadata and SHA256 where applicable
  + validation rejects nonregular symlinked or hash-drifted executables and files and canonicalizes directories
  + ChildTransport directly owns one child with piped stdin bounded concurrent stdout and stderr readers JSONL line and total-byte limits deadline handling and Drop termination plus wait
  + session code emits initialize then initialized and strictly parses expected response and event shapes
  + returned thread authority is checked for approval policy never readOnly sandbox no unexpected network access and exact canonical working directory
  + server requests forbidden item types extra calls malformed events oversized streams timeout early EOF and partial terminal states refuse
  + these mechanics are useful design evidence but the private carrier has no independent B1 authority and cannot be imported by assertion

& [NonReusableLiveSemantics]
  + LiveCodexConfig validation launches the executable with --version before constructing the driver
  + ChildTransport inherits the ambient process environment because its Command does not call env_clear
  + the app-server command configures a required Cantor MCP subprocess and passes a real environment file path
  + session code creates an ephemeral thread then starts a model turn with a prompt and output schema
  + the turn is expected to call one MCP tool and therefore exercises provider model and MCP behavior outside the B1 provider-free preflight boundary
  + it uses the admitted working directory but has no separate disposable CODEX_HOME CODEX_SQLITE_HOME evidence-root canary-root or recovery-owner contract
  + it confirms returned sandbox metadata but does not independently attempt and remeasure denied host effects
  + it has no command/exec-only method-closed protocol state and cannot make shellCommand process/spawn or other generated-schema methods unrepresentable

& [B1CarrierCandidate]
  + retain direct absolute executable launch child ownership piped JSONL bounded dual-stream drain deadline interruption termination wait and late-output accounting
  + replace open JSON Value method emission with a closed internal state machine that can emit only initialize initialized bounded configuration reads and one command/exec probe
  + omit thread/start turn/start MCP configuration environment file prompt output schema provider model and tool-call event handling
  + bind exact generated request response notification and error schemas for the selected executable and reject unknown fields methods ids ordering duplicates and messages after terminal state
  + apply the env_clear-first grammar disposable state roots and canary observer from the separately preserved environment and sandbox inventories
  + rehash the executable immediately before every launch and account for the outer child and every observed descendant before accepting termination
  + do not expose a generic send method raw method string arbitrary JSON command argv shell expansion or transport constructor outside the B1 module

& [Delineation]
  + existing live_codex proves a strict carrier is feasible with current dependencies but does not authorize reusing its provider-contacting session
  + mechanical pattern reuse is not source-code reuse and exact extraction or duplication shape remains an SJS design decision
  + a readOnly response is a correspondence check while independent canary post-state remains the enforcement proof
  + process ownership of the outer child is not descendant-account proof until the selected App Server behavior is independently observed

& [GapDelta]
  + G05 changes from an unspecified carrier to an exact predecessor inventory reusable mechanics forbidden semantics and a bounded command/exec-only candidate
  + G05 remains unresolved for selected-version generated schemas exact Rust type placement descendant enumeration terminal grammar and implementation support matrix
  + G03 G04 and G06 remain narrowed_not_closed under their separate inventories
  + G01 selection G02 exact schema and G07 live evidence remain open

& [StopRules]
  + do not launch validate instantiate modify extract or repurpose LiveCodexConfig StdioAppServerDriver ChildTransport or run_app_server_session
  + do not invoke --version app-server thread turn MCP provider model tool environment file or working-directory observation
  + do not treat existing tests mock transcripts readOnly metadata or content-addressed evidence as B1 live process or enforcement proof
  + do not broaden B1 with a generic JSON-RPC transport or public process capability

